<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys 150,000T French wheat for Jan load.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys 150,000T French wheat for Jan load.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's General Authority for Supply Commodities (GASC) said on Saturday it was buying 150,000 tonnes of French soft red wheat. GASC vice chairman Samir Shakankiri told Reuters the breakdown was:</p>
<p>- 50,000 tonnes at $149.50 FOB from Dreyfus for loading in January.</p>
<p>- 50,000 tonnes at $149.75 FOB from Soufflet for loading in the second half of January.</p>
<p>- 50,000 tonnes at $149.89 from Romak for loading in January.</p>
<p>-- Christine Hauser +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
